{"paths": ["governance/INDIA8_REGIE_READINESS_AUDIT_2026-08-23.md"], "blob_sha": "bf71d0b8a8d3aaf09affe9280caee3af23eeda68", "original_offset": 0, "original_length": 3906, "final_blob_size": 3906, "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_count": 1, "classification": "text", "content_utf8": "# INDIA8 REGIE READINESS AUDIT — 2026-08-23\n\nStatus: REGIE_READY_WITH_BOUNDED_EXTERNAL_CHECKS\nOwner: INDIA8\n\n## CONCLUSIE\nINDIA8 heeft de repository opnieuw repositorybreed gereconcilieerd voor reisregie na de canon-miss van 2026-08-23. De regie mag inhoudelijk doorgaan, mits onderstaande precedence/bootregels worden gevolgd.\n\nEr is GEEN bekende verborgen autonome regietaak meer die alleen als prose-'later' is blijven liggen.\n\n## WAT NU SCHERP / GESLOTEN IS\n1. Reisdata: 18-12-2026 t/m 21-01-2027 = 34 dagen; retour Delhi.\n2. Actuele clusterstatus:\n   - Kumaon A\n   - Vrindavan/Braj/Mathura A route-sensitive\n   - Varanasi/Sarnath A\n   - Bodh Gaya/Gaya A\n   - Tiruvannamalai/Arunachala A fixed\n   - Agra A Taj-only, sunrise hard\n   - Haridwar/Kankhal/Rishikesh B/reserve\n   - Mysore/Bengaluru C\n   - Oost/Kolkata parked\n3. Bekende slaapbases/anchor-zones:\n   - Joshi Guest House locked\n   - Hotel Evelyn anchor + A\n   - Turiya Niwas provisional sleep lock + A\n   - Sahi River View Guesthouse LOCKED_BY_MARK\n   - Vrindavan proper anchor zone resolved\n   - Bodh Gaya Mahabodhi-core zone resolved\n   - Tiruvannamalai Ramana Nagar/Ramanasramam zone resolved\n   - Agra East Gate/Taj Ganj positioning zone resolved\n4. Kumaon three-base execution matrix built; old A/C canon protected.\n5. CCI Lonely Planet high-threshold gapcheck integrated: 3 additive misses only.\n6. Critical boot/no-deferral governance installed and root README made mandatory gate.\n7. Final INDIA8->INDIA9 boot handoff exists and supersedes conflicting older immediate-action sections.\n8. Hotel Evelyn comfort preference corrected: heritage authenticity > comfort; poor maintenance/heating cost does not demote it.\n\n## EXTERNE CHECKS DIE BEWUST LOPEN / KLAARSTAAN\nThese are not hidden regie omissions; they are independent evidence-expansion tasks.\n\n### A. Hotel Evelyn targeted closure\nTask:\n`runs/active/INDIA8-HOTEL-EVELYN-RAMDASS-ROOM-CLOSURE-001/TASK.md`\nGoal: exact room/floor/wing/balcony/patio closure through independent source/photo investigation. Do not invent room number.\nUse a color worker, not CCI, to conserve CCI tokens.\n\n### B. Lonely Planet second opinion — two workers\nTask:\n`runs/active/INDIA8-LONELYPLANET-SECOND-OPINION-001/TASK.md`\nWorker A: micro-gems/human traveler signal.\nWorker B: nature/landscape/archaeology outliers.\nMaximum 10 additive findings each; 0 valid. Existing 80 + CCI-3 may not be duplicated.\n\n## CCI ROLE FROM HERE\nDo NOT ask CCI for another full Lonely Planet sweep now. Existing CCI high-threshold gapcheck found only 3 evident misses, proving diminishing returns.\n\nUse CCI next only when one of these occurs:\n1. second-opinion workers return materially conflicting/additive findings that need independent adjudication;\n2. route/accounting integration needs a global crosscheck;\n3. a high-impact historical identity/access conflict remains after color research.\n\nCCI is QA/reconciliation, not bulk discovery.\n\n## WAT NOG OPEN MAG BLIJVEN\nOnly these categories may remain open without violating NO-DEFERRAL:\n- explicit Mark A/B/C or hotel/property choice;\n- live availability/price/booking when exact date is not fixed;\n- calendar facts requiring authoritative 2027 schedules not yet published/resolved;\n- independent worker tasks above that INDIA8 cannot execute as a separate model itself.\n\n## HARD PRESENTATION RULE\nBefore presenting ANY candidate/location/hotel/cluster:\n`LATEST MARK DECISION -> LOCKED_BY_MARK/ACCOMMODATION -> CLUSTER DECISION -> SITE A/B/C -> CURRENT MASTER -> GOVERNANCE -> LEGACY PROTECTED CANON -> NEW DELTA`.\n\nIf already decided, do not ask again. Present only new delta.\n\n## CURRENT IMMEDIATE REGIE DIRECTION\nRegie may continue now. It does not need to wait for the bounded workers.\nUse existing sleep bases and cluster canon to continue cluster-by-cluster travel construction and Lonely-Planet selection. Integrate worker returns additively when they arrive.\n"}
